.\" Manual page for ytmplayer. Plain man(7) macros, so groff and mandoc both render it.
.\" Options listed here are the ones `ytmplayer --help` prints (USAGE in src/main.rs);
.\" a flag added to one belongs in the other.
.TH YTMPLAYER 1 2026-11-21 ytmplayer "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytmplayer \- terminal music player for YouTube, SoundCloud, Spotify links and local files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytmplayer
.RB [ \-\-shuffle ]
.RB [ \-\-volume
.IR level ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ url " | " path " | " "search words" ...]
.br
.B ytmplayer
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.br
.B ytmplayer
.BR \-V " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ytmplayer
plays audio in a full-screen, fully clickable text interface, with a play queue,
live audio scopes, an effects rack, an equalizer, beat-matched transitions, a local
library, background downloads, and the video itself as true-colour ASCII on demand.
It drives
.BR mpv (1)
for playback and
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
for resolving links.
.PP
The one argument says what to play:
.TP
.I url
A YouTube or SoundCloud track, playlist, album, set or station, or a Spotify
track, album or playlist.
Spotify audio is never streamed: each track is matched on YouTube by name.
Quote a URL that contains
.BR & ,
or the shell will cut it there.
.TP
.I path
A media file, a folder, or an
.BR .m3u ", " .m3u8 " or " .pls
list.
A folder is played with everything beneath it, in path order, so albums stay
together and in track order.
Hidden files and folders are skipped.
A leading
.B ~
is expanded.
Anything that begins with
.BR / ", " ~ ", " ./ " or " ../
is taken for a path whether or not it exists, and one that is not there is an
error rather than a search.
.TP
.I search words
Anything that is neither a link nor a path is searched for on YouTube.
The first hit plays and the rest wait in the queue.
Several words need no quotes:
.B ytmplayer boards of canada roygbiv
is one search.
.PP
With no argument
.B ytmplayer
opens a URL bar: type or paste a link, a path or a search there, or press
.B Tab
to resume the previous session where it stopped.
.PP
A session started with an argument ends when its queue runs out.
One started bare stays open until it is quit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-shuffle
Start with the queue in a random order.
.TP
.BI \-\-volume " level"
Starting volume, from 0 to 150.
100 is the track's own level.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and keys on standard output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version on standard output and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options.
Whatever follows is the thing to play, even if it begins with a dash.
.PP
An option that is not one of these is an error:
the usage is printed on standard error and nothing is played.
.SH KEYS
Every key shown on screen in parentheses is also a button.
.SS Main view
.PD 0
.TP 22
.B Space
Play or pause.
.TP
.BR h ", " l " or " Left ", " Right
Seek back or forward 5 seconds.
.TP
.BR j ", " k " or " Down ", " Up
Volume down or up.
.TP
.BR n ", " b
Next or previous track.
.TP
.B v
Choose what the centre panel shows: queue, scope, video or library.
.TP
.B p
Show the queue there straight away.
.TP
.B o
Add a link, a path or a search; it plays after the current track.
.TP
.B d
Save the current track into
.IR downloads/ .
Pressing it again cancels.
.TP
.B e
Effects rack.
.TP
.B g
Equalizer.
.TP
.B s
Settings.
.TP
.BR q " or " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.PD
.SS Queue in the centre panel
.PD 0
.TP 22
.BR Up ", " Down ", " PgUp ", " PgDn
Move the cursor.
.TP
.B Enter
Play the selected track.
.TP
.B E
Reorder mode;
.BR J " and " K
then move the selected track down or up.
.TP
.B a
Save the whole queue.
Pressing it again cancels.
.PD
.SS Library in the centre panel
.PD 0
.TP 22
.B /
Filter as you type;
.B Esc
leaves the filter.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down ", " PgUp ", " PgDn
Move the cursor.
.TP
.B Enter
Play the selected track next.
.TP
.B +
Add it to the end of the queue instead.
.TP
.B R
Index
.I ~/Music
and
.IR downloads/ .
.TP
.B A
Add another folder to the index.
.PD
.SS View chooser
.PD 0
.TP 22
.BR j ", " k
Move.
.TP
.BR Enter " or " Space
Show the selected panel.
.TP
.BR h ", " l
Change the style of the scope.
.TP
.BR v " or " Esc
Back out, leaving the panel as it was.
.PD
.SS Settings, effects and equalizer
.PD 0
.TP 22
.BR j ", " k
Move.
.TP
.BR h ", " l
Change the selected setting.
.TP
.BR Enter " or " Space
Switch the selected effect, or apply the selected equalizer preset.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Close.
Settings are saved on the way out.
.PD
.SS URL bar
.PD 0
.TP 22
.B Enter
Open what was typed.
.TP
.B Tab
Resume the previous session.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel; on the opening screen, quit.
.PD
.SH MOUSE
The progress bar seeks where it is clicked.
The volume rail on the right sets the level where it is clicked.
Queue rows jump to their track.
Clicking the centre panel steps it to the next view.
The wheel scrolls the queue when the pointer is over it, and turns the volume
everywhere else.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ytmplayer/config
Settings, as
.IB key = value
lines, written by the settings view.
.I ~/.config
is used when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ytmplayer/transitions/*.mix
Your own transitions.
The format is described in
.IR WRITING\-TRANSITIONS.md ,
and the built-in ones are installed as examples in
.IR /usr/share/ytmplayer/transitions/ .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ytmplayer/
What the player remembers: where the last session stopped, what has been played,
the library index, measured tempos, and where saved tracks went.
.I ~/.local/state
is used when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is not set.
Removing the directory resets all of it.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ytmplayer/bin/yt\-dlp
The player's own copy of
.BR yt\-dlp ,
when it holds one.
See
.BR "KEEPING YT\-DLP CURRENT" .
.TP
.I ./downloads/
Saved tracks, in the directory
.B ytmplayer
was started from.
.SH KEEPING YT\-DLP CURRENT
Sites change what they serve every few weeks,
.B yt\-dlp
follows within days, and a copy that is months old stops resolving links.
So the first time a session needs
.B yt\-dlp
\(en at most once a day, and never for a session that only plays local files \(en
.B ytmplayer
asks GitHub which release is the latest.
When neither the installed
.B yt\-dlp
nor the player's own copy is that recent, it downloads the release with
.BR curl (1)
into the state directory, checks it against the checksum the release publishes
(with
.BR sha256sum (1)
or
.BR shasum (1))
and that it runs, and uses it from then on,
for its own lookups and for
.BR mpv 's.
.PP
A machine with no
.B yt\-dlp
at all is given one the same way.
Once the system's own
.B yt\-dlp
has caught up, the player's copy is deleted and the system's is used again.
If the check or the download fails \(en no network, no
.B curl
\(en whatever
.B yt\-dlp
already worked keeps being used.
.PP
The small release file needs Python 3; without one the larger self-contained
build is fetched instead.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings and your transitions live.
Default
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Where history, the resume point, the library index and the player's
.B yt\-dlp
live.
Default
.IR ~/.local/state .
.TP
.B PATH
Searched for
.BR mpv ", " yt\-dlp ", " ffmpeg ", " ffprobe ", " curl ", " sha256sum " and " shasum .
.TP
.BR TERM ", " TERM_PROGRAM ", " KITTY_WINDOW_ID ", " TMUX
Decide how cover art is drawn: as a real picture on terminals that implement
the kitty graphics protocol, and as coloured half-blocks everywhere else,
including inside
.BR tmux (1).
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus the player registers on, so media keys and
.BR playerctl (1)
can control it.
Without a session bus that integration is simply absent.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.BR mpv (1)
Required.
It decodes and plays everything.
.TP
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
Required for links and searches, not for local files.
Fetched and updated automatically, as described above.
For YouTube it needs a JavaScript runtime of its own;
.BR deno (1)
is the one it looks for by default.
.TP
.BR curl (1)
Fetches
.B yt\-dlp
and reads Spotify links.
.TP
.BR ffmpeg "(1), " ffprobe (1)
Optional.
Saving tracks as MP3 or above, cover art, the library's tags, and the
measurements beat-matched transitions rely on.
.PP
The terminal needs true colour for the scopes and the video, and should be at
least 44 columns by 20 rows for them; smaller terminals get the text interface
without them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The session ended normally, or
.B \-\-help
or
.B \-\-version
was asked for.
.TP
.B 1
Something could not be played or started:
an unknown option, a path that does not exist, a link that did not resolve,
a missing program, or output that is not a terminal.
The reason is printed on standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
ytmplayer "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ"
ytmplayer boards of canada roygbiv
ytmplayer ~/Music \-\-shuffle
ytmplayer \-\-volume 60 "https://soundcloud.com/artist/sets/album"
ytmplayer "https://open.spotify.com/playlist/37i9dQZF1DXcBWIGoYBM5M"
ytmplayer
.RE
.fi
.SH BUGS
Report them at
.IR https://github.com/Osyna/YTM\-Player/issues .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR playerctl (1)
